{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I've revised the report for both round-2 findings, and it passes the mechanical check with no verdicts. Finding f1.2 is only partly fixed: no block or appendix table can show the pooled quality scores.

- **f1.2 (pooled quality not in a block):** the headline's "closes most of the gap" now rests on figures written into c1's sentence: each model's pooled overall quality and each step's gain with its interval. Neither c1's block nor the appendix table can show pooled scores. I tried listing all four models in the price table; it still shows only the price per point. I logged the gap. Open-70B's pooled score now appears under "Why not". Method says the full-results tables hold per-task scores only, and where each pooled score appears instead.
- **f2.1 (Open-70B dismissed on point estimates):** "Why not" now leads with Open-70B's behaviour: it confirms before account changes less often than any other model (81%). It then says Open-70B is off the frontier on point estimates only. Its gain over Brisk-S is +0.79, with an interval of −0.19 to +1.77 that includes zero. At the interval's top, a point bought by moving to it would cost as little as $3.11, which falls in Brisk-S's price range. The explore row says the same, and the no-control caveat now names this gap as one a paired read could separate.

